<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto II, Duke of Merania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1248</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto II was the last Duke of Merania and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from the house of Andechs. His family had lost lands after being accused of involvement in the murder of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a> in 1208. When he died childless in 1248, the Andechs lands were divided among the Wittelsbachs, the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> and other heirs.</p></div>
